// Not supported yet: a closure that captures, written in a LOW function. The closure object has to go
// somewhere and LOW does not allocate (how it would is undecided). Capturing nothing is fine: see
// 26_closure_low. (Calling a closure that LOW did not create is refused by sema, TIER-017:
// tests/fixtures/err_closure_tier_low_param.ubl.)
// expect-refusal: a closure that captures a variable in `@tier(low)`
@tier(low)
fn run(k: int) int {
    let f = fn(x: int) x + k
    return f(1)
}

fn main() void {
    println(run(2))
}
